{
  "description": "Bounded execution-report trimming (OBS-R41, OBS-R110): when a report's compact UTF-8 JSON (OBS-R42) exceeds maximumBytes, the oldest tool-call record is removed first, the oldest error only after no tool-call record remains, and truncated becomes true; the result is the first report of that sequence that fits. bytes is the size of the untrimmed report; each limit gives the retained suffixes (toolCallsFrom, errorsFrom), truncated and the retained size, or aggregateTooLarge when even the report without detail exceeds the limit. The limits are every size of the removal sequence, that size minus one byte and the untrimmed size plus one. Go checks telemetry Policy.NormalizeExecutionReport, Python telemetry.metrics.trim_report_detail. The reports use only content both models render identically: integers, no empty arguments object, no completion block.",
